-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §viewport-media-queries — the shell's layout steps use viewport width
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Decision: the shell's layout steps use viewport `@media (min-width: 720px)` queries; container queries are dropped.
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport (user overrode it on 2026-10-23, following a team decision in sync: half the
+  team has never used container queries).
+- Known trade-off: the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen, so the two-column
+  layout can again be chosen inside a narrow pane and clip the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14). Accepted by the maintainer.
+
+### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width (SUPERSEDED 2026-10-23 by §viewport-media-queries)
 - Since: 2026-09-15
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
